+### Actions
+
+Actions choose the class of the object a rule builds. They are written in
+braces and may be used anywhere in a rule body:
+
+- `{Class}` - an object of `Class` becomes the object being built.
+- `{Class.attr=current}` - an object of `Class` becomes the object being built
+  and the object built so far is assigned to its `attr`.
+- `{Class.attr+=current}` - the same, but the object built so far is appended
+  to the list `attr`.
+
+Assignments after an action fill the new object and the rule returns the object
+that is current when the rule finishes. This makes it easy to build
+left-associative expression trees:
+
+    Sum: Product ({Add.left=current} '+' right=Product
+                 | {Sub.left=current} '-' right=Product)*;
+    Product: Number ({Mul.left=current} '*' right=Number)*;
+    Number: value=INT;
+
+For the input `1 + 2 * 3 - 4`, `Sum` returns a `Sub` whose `left` is an `Add`
+and whose `right` is the `Number` 4.
+
+If `Class` is not a rule of the grammar, a new class inheriting from the rule is
+created. Attributes are registered on the classes whose objects receive them
+and multiplicities are decided per object.
+
+
 ## Repetition modifiers
 
 Repetition modifiers are used for the modification of the repetition expressions
